/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  Feature edges, one .eMesh per STL, read by snappy's `features` entry. Copy into
  <case>/system/ and run `surfaceFeatureExtract` before snappyHexMesh.

  The utility installed here is `surfaceFeatureExtract`, so this file is
  `surfaceFeatureExtractDict`; the older `surfaceFeatures`/`surfaceFeaturesDict`
  pair, which took a flat `surfaces (...)` list, is not in v2512.

  One block per surface. patch_entries.py --insert writes the blocks from what is in
  constant/triSurface/, so the block list and the geometry list cannot drift apart.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      surfaceFeatureExtractDict;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

// includedAngle 150: an edge is a feature when the two triangles either side of it
// meet at less than this. 180 takes every edge in the tessellation, 0 takes none;
// 150 keeps a box corner (90) and a fillet break and drops the facet seams a curved
// wall is tessellated into. Lower it towards 100 on a shape whose creases are shallow.

